{
  "Makes any content movable with the pointer, touch or the arrow keys, optionally along one axis, inside a boundary, by a handle or as a copy. `DropTarget` defines areas that accept it. To reorder items in a list, see [Sortable](/sortable).": "",
  "Moving content": "",
  "JSX children are the movable content. `boundary` keeps it inside its parent or an element, `axis` limits it to one direction, and `handle` sets the only part that responds to the pointer and keyboard. A drag writes the position to `x-model`, `onDragEnded` reports it, and Escape returns the content to its start.": "",
  "Drop targets": "Bırakma hedefleri",
  "A `DropTarget` in the same `group` accepts a draggable dropped on it and receives the draggable's `data` in `onDropped`. `onDragEntering` can reject it. With `clone`, a copy follows the pointer and the original stays, so one item can be dropped many times. Your code decides what a drop does to your data.": "",
  "`position` sets the location in pixels from the element's layout position, and `x-model` receives it after every drag or key press, so you can save and restore it.": "",
  "The draggable, or its handle, is one Tab stop.": "",
  "Moves it by `step` pixels along its axis and inside its boundary, and the new position is announced.": "",
  "During a drag, cancels it and returns the item to where it started.": "",
  "A `group` with `aria-roledescription=\"draggable\"`, named “Move” in the kit language. With a `handle`, that element is a button with this name instead.": "",
  "A long press lifts it on a touch screen. During a drag, it lets pointer events pass through so the target underneath can be detected, and a `clone` copy follows the pointer.": "",
  "Marked while a drag from their group is active, while the draggable is over them, and when they reject it.": "",
  "The draggable. `data-dragging`, `data-handle`, `data-clone`, `data-axis`.": "Draggable. `data-dragging`, `data-handle`, `data-clone`, `data-axis`.",
  "The handle specified by `handle`, and the copy that follows the pointer.": "",
  "A target. `data-drop-active` during a drag from its group, `data-drop-over`, `data-drop-refused`.": "",
  "Units: the draggable (`draggable`, `dragging`, `focus`), its handle (`hover`, `focus`) and the copy.": "",
  "Unit: a target (`active`, `over`, `refused`).": "Unit: hedef (`active`, `over`, `refused`).",
  "Draggable props": "Draggable prop'ları",
  "`both`, `x` or `y`.": "`both`, `x` ya da `y`.",
  "The area it stays inside: its parent, or an element that contains it.": "",
  "A selector inside the draggable. Only this part starts a drag, and it receives the Tab stop and keyboard input.": "",
  "A copy follows the pointer and the draggable stays in place, ready to be dropped on a target.": "",
  "Drop targets in the same group accept it.": "",
  "Custom data passed to the drop target on drop.": "",
  "The number of pixels an arrow key moves it.": "",
  "The position in pixels from its layout position. When set, it is applied, and after every drag or key press the new position is written to `x-model`.": "",
  "DropTarget props and events": "DropTarget prop'ları ve event'leri",
  "Accepts draggables in this group. `null` accepts those without a group.": "",
  "Occurs when a draggable enters (`draggable`, `data`). Set `cancel = true` to reject it.": "",
  "Occurs when the draggable leaves.": "",
  "Occurs when a draggable is dropped on it. Your code moves the data.": "",
  "Occurs before a drag starts. Set `cancel = true` to keep it in place.": "",
  "Occurs during a drag (`x`, `y`, and the `target` under the pointer).": "",
  "Occurs when the pointer is released. Set `cancel = true` to return it to where it started.": "",
  "Occurs when the drag ends (`x`, `y`, `target`, `dropped`).": "",
  "The current position.": "",
  "Indicates that a drag is in progress.": "",
  "The element that handles the pointer and keyboard: the handle, or the draggable itself.": ""
}
